About the rates: each is a Wilson interval, and a finding is kept when its lower
bound clears the threshold. Sampling stops as soon as the interval is decisive,
so it is not a calibrated 95% interval; the decision it supports errs towards
dropping a real finding rather than keeping a spurious one.
